## battlecode/battlecode24 — the 2024 rules, constants, maps and sprites

Repository: <https://github.com/battlecode/battlecode24>, pinned at commit
`166c79bbf4156c866caf434062cb1f403c01695f`.

**The ENGINE is AGPL-3.0** — verified: `engine/COPYING` is the GNU Affero
General Public License v3, and so is `schema/LICENSE`. **The repository root
carries no LICENSE file.** What derives from the engine, named individually:

* `src/battlecode/years/bc24/**` — the 2024 rule set, hand-ported to Nim as a
  BEHAVIOUR port from `world/GameWorld.java`, `world/InternalRobot.java`,
  `world/RobotControllerImpl.java`, `world/TeamInfo.java`, `world/Flag.java`,
  `world/Trap.java`, `world/ObjectInfo.java` and `world/LiveMap.java`.
* `src/battlecode/years/bc24/constants.nim` — GENERATED by
  `tools/gen_year_constants.py --year bc24` from `common/GameConstants.java`,
  `common/SkillType.java`, `common/TrapType.java` and
  `common/GlobalUpgrade.java`.
* `data/maps/bc24/*.json` — the 22 converted maps, read out of the official
  `.map24` flatbuffers in `engine/src/main/battlecode/world/resources/`.
* `data/bc24/skills.json` — generated from the engine's own arithmetic, under
  a JDK, from the released jar's own classes.
* `src/battlecode/years/bc24/chassis/scaffold24.nim` — `examplefuncsplayer`,
  ported statement for statement from
  `example-bots/src/main/examplefuncsplayer/RobotPlayer.java`. It is the
  parity oracle's other side and may not gain behaviour.
* `tools/oracle/bc24/Bc24Trace.java` — a trace driver written against the
  engine's own package-private API, compiled ONLY in CI.

**The CLIENT SPRITES are GPL-3.0, and the client has no LICENSE file of its
own.** `client/package.json` declares `"license": "GPL-3.0"`; unlike
battlecode21, whose `client/LICENSE` was the AGPL, the 2024 client directory
carries no licence file, so the `package.json` declaration is the whole of
what upstream states. `data/atlas_bc24.png` and `data/atlas_bc24.json` are cut
by `tools/build_sprite_atlas_bc24.py` from 25 PNGs under
`client/src/static/img/`:

* `robots/brown/{base,attack,build,heal,jailed}.png` and the `white/` set,
* `traps/{brown,white}/{explosive,stun,water}.png` and the untinted
  `traps/{explosive,stun,water}.png`,
* `resources/{bread,bread_outline,bread_outline_thick,crumb_1,crumb_2,crumb_3}.png`.

GPLv3 §13 and AGPLv3 §13 expressly permit the combination of GPL-3.0 and
AGPL-3.0 works, which is exactly what this repository is. The repository as a
whole remains AGPL-3.0 and this NOTICE records the sprite files' own terms.
(`schema/package.json` also says `GPL-3.0` while `schema/LICENSE` is the AGPL;
the discrepancy is recorded and is moot here, because NO SCHEMA CODE IS USED
AT ALL — there is no flatbuffers reader on either side of this port.)

**The engine itself is used only at CI time.** No JDK, no JRE and no upstream
Java source or bytecode exists in any image this repository builds.

The published `battlecode24-3.0.5.jar`
(<https://releases.battlecode.org/maven/org/battlecode/battlecode24/3.0.5/battlecode24-3.0.5.jar>,
sha256 pinned in `tools/oracle/bc24/jar.lock`) is downloaded by the
`parity-oracle-bc24` CI job and is never redistributed here.

